  "term": "alcohol-induced persisting amnestic disorder",
  "definition": "Alcohol-induced persisting amnestic disorder is a long-lasting memory disorder linked to chronic alcohol misuse and related nutritional deficiency. It mainly involves short-term memory loss, often with made-up memories used to fill gaps, along with problems with attention.",
